1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:01,633
<i>I won't be home
for the next few days.</i>

2
00:00:01,767 --> 00:00:03,267
<i> Your meeting seems important.</i>

3
00:00:03,400 --> 00:00:04,633
<i> Is there a problem, Mom?</i>

4
00:00:04,767 --> 00:00:08,600
<i>How can I help you if you don't
tell me what the problem is?</i>

5
00:00:08,733 --> 00:00:09,600
<i> He's here.</i>

6
00:00:09,733 --> 00:00:12,300
<i>Maybe you've heard a new name?
Berdugo.</i>

7
00:00:12,433 --> 00:00:14,400
<i>Berdugo?
I just heard that name today.</i>

8
00:00:14,533 --> 00:00:16,500
<i>Someone here is asking
about Berdugo.</i>

9
00:00:16,633 --> 00:00:18,067
<i>That's our boss's name,
isn't it, Sir?</i>

10
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:19,967
<i>Find out who's asking
about Berdugo.</i>

11
00:00:20,100 --> 00:00:22,667
<i>My child Joey,
are you back at the dorm yet?</i>

12
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:24,600
<i> You didn't update me.</i>

13
00:00:24,733 --> 00:00:26,867
<i>I was tired last night.
I fell asleep.</i>

14
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:29,000
<i> That's why you and Peter
haven't seen each other, right?</i>

15
00:00:29,133 --> 00:00:30,033
<i> Peter?</i>

16
00:00:30,167 --> 00:00:31,167
<i> Hello, Peter?</i>

17
00:00:31,300 --> 00:00:32,867
<i>Joey, I'm glad I talked to you.
Where are you?</i>

18
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:35,633
<i>Andrew and I are following
a lead.</i>

19
00:00:35,800 --> 00:00:37,867
<i>There's this woman
under my radar.</i>

20
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:38,967
<i> It's Delilah.</i>

21
00:00:39,100 --> 00:00:40,433
<i> She's the one suspected</i>

22
00:00:40,567 --> 00:00:43,033
<i>of being in charge of drug
distribution here in Valmora.</i>

23
00:00:43,167 --> 00:00:46,433
<i>You know, if Berdugo will meet
someone here, it might be her.</i>

24
00:00:46,567 --> 00:00:47,533
<i> That's good.</i>

25
00:00:47,667 --> 00:00:48,967
<i>She owns several businesses
here in Valmora.</i>

26
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:51,400
<i>One of them is the new
Nature Hotel and Resort.</i>

27
00:00:51,533 --> 00:00:53,800
<i>Okay, I'll check in there
to investigate.</i>

28
00:00:53,933 --> 00:00:55,700
<i>Just stay put.
I'll take care of it.</i>

29
00:00:55,833 --> 00:00:57,733
<i>Boss Delilah, I'll return
your money right away.</i>

30
00:00:57,867 --> 00:00:58,933
<i> I'll find a way!</i>

31
00:00:59,067 --> 00:01:00,733
<i>You should have done
that a long time ago.</i>

32
00:01:00,867 --> 00:01:02,933
<i>- I'm sorry.
- Boss, don't.</i>

33
00:01:04,067 --> 00:01:06,133
<i>So what? Are we really
at a dead end here?</i>

34
00:01:06,267 --> 00:01:09,600
<i>Has "Joey On Duty" lost her
courage?l</i>

35
00:01:09,767 --> 00:01:11,033
<i> But what are we going to do?</i>

36
00:01:11,167 --> 00:01:12,633
<i>Actually,
I've thought of something.</i>

37
00:01:12,767 --> 00:01:14,167
<i>I just don't know
if you'll agree.</i>

38
00:01:14,300 --> 00:01:15,433
<i> Okay, I'm game.</i>

39
00:01:44,300 --> 00:01:46,167
What are you doinlg here?

40
00:01:46,300 --> 00:01:47,867
Boss Idol!

41
00:01:55,967 --> 00:01:56,900
Hi.

42
00:01:57,033 --> 00:02:00,533
I called earlier for a suite.

43
00:02:00,667 --> 00:02:02,067
Hold on...

44
00:02:03,200 --> 00:02:04,833
Here's my card.

45
00:02:06,933 --> 00:02:12,467
Wow. You're something else.
You even booked a couple's room.

46
00:02:12,600 --> 00:02:15,033
Of course, only the best
for my girlfriend.

47
00:02:29,867 --> 00:02:32,533
You're in trouble,
your ex seems affected.

48
00:02:35,467 --> 00:02:37,533
I'll explain to her
when I get the chance.

49
00:02:37,667 --> 00:02:40,967
That's our only way to be near
the subject.

50
00:02:42,467 --> 00:02:43,600
Boss Idol...

51
00:02:43,733 --> 00:02:46,267
- I mean, Mr. Dizon.
- Yes?

52
00:02:46,400 --> 00:02:48,100
Here's your card and key.

53
00:02:48,267 --> 00:02:51,200
I got you the best room
for couples, Sir.

54
00:02:51,333 --> 00:02:52,667
Thank you.

55
00:02:54,533 --> 00:02:56,933
By the way,
how's the security here?

56
00:02:57,067 --> 00:03:01,000
You're safe here, Boss Idol.
We have CCTVs.

57
00:03:01,133 --> 00:03:04,767
Even though there's no guard,
they're recording 24/7.

58
00:03:04,900 --> 00:03:09,067
But don't worry, Boss Idol.
The people here are nice.

59
00:03:10,667 --> 00:03:11,833
Like you, right?

60
00:03:11,967 --> 00:03:13,300
You're very nice.

61
00:03:13,433 --> 00:03:14,467
Yes.

62
00:03:14,600 --> 00:03:16,200
Anyway, okay, thank you.

63
00:03:17,367 --> 00:03:20,567
Let's check the couple's room?

64
00:03:24,733 --> 00:03:26,100
Francis.

65
00:03:26,233 --> 00:03:27,600
Clean that up.

66
00:03:29,733 --> 00:03:30,633
Yes, Madam.

67
00:03:31,733 --> 00:03:33,733
Aren't you used to it by now?

68
00:03:33,867 --> 00:03:36,067
We've been doing that
for a long time.

69
00:03:37,967 --> 00:03:41,933
Send a big suitcase here
to Madam's room.

70
00:03:42,067 --> 00:03:43,167
Please hurry.

71
00:03:43,300 --> 00:03:44,500
<i> Copy.</i>

72
00:03:44,633 --> 00:03:46,000
Thank you.

73
00:03:47,933 --> 00:03:50,133
Why do you look pale?

74
00:03:51,167 --> 00:03:53,967
Remember, this is what we do.

75
00:03:54,100 --> 00:03:56,567
So you just have to get used
to it,

76
00:03:56,733 --> 00:03:59,633
especially from those who take
advantage of us.

77
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:12,433
<i> What were you thinking?</i>

78
00:04:12,567 --> 00:04:13,667
Didn't I tell you...

79
00:04:13,800 --> 00:04:15,500
<i>Zoey, didn't I tell you
to be quiet?</i>

80
00:04:15,633 --> 00:04:17,367
There's a CCTV camera there.

81
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:21,900
Didn't I tell you to stay home?
My mission might be jeopardized.

82
00:04:22,033 --> 00:04:23,867
Look. We won't be in your way.

83
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:25,400
Do your mission,

84
00:04:25,533 --> 00:04:29,033
and Joey and I will do
our strategy.

85
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:33,033
What, for you to flirt with your
girlfriend while I do the job?

86
00:04:33,167 --> 00:04:35,900
We have our own investigation,

87
00:04:36,033 --> 00:04:38,533
and the only way to keep people
from suspecting me,

88
00:04:38,667 --> 00:04:40,100
even if they see me,

89
00:04:40,233 --> 00:04:45,567
is to show them that I am
on vacation, okay?

90
00:04:45,700 --> 00:04:47,467
You know, whatever you're
planning,

91
00:04:47,600 --> 00:04:50,200
don't continue with it.
Get out of here now.

92
00:04:52,600 --> 00:04:55,267
If this is what I need to do
to help my father,

93
00:04:55,400 --> 00:04:57,367
to find him, I will do it.

94
00:04:57,500 --> 00:04:59,200
<i> You can't get me out of here.</i>

95
00:04:59,333 --> 00:05:01,833
If you want, arrest me.

96
00:05:08,367 --> 00:05:11,133
Just make sure you don't ruin
my plan.

97
00:05:13,833 --> 00:05:15,000
Okay.

98
00:05:28,300 --> 00:05:30,333
How long will it take?

99
00:05:30,467 --> 00:05:32,167
It's been a few days.

100
00:05:32,300 --> 00:05:35,633
To this day, we still haven't
seen my husband's remains.

101
00:05:37,000 --> 00:05:39,933
To be honest,
even I am getting frustrated.

102
00:05:40,067 --> 00:05:42,600
I know this is hard
for your family,

103
00:05:42,733 --> 00:05:46,467
but we have to follow the
protocol of the investigation.

104
00:05:46,600 --> 00:05:49,867
Chief, damn those protocols!

105
00:05:50,000 --> 00:05:52,233
My husband has been burned,

106
00:05:52,367 --> 00:05:55,233
and yet you won't leave him
in peace!

107
00:05:55,367 --> 00:05:57,567
I'm really sorry, Mrs. Delgado.

108
00:05:57,700 --> 00:06:03,300
Clarissa, but all I can do
is follow up and wait.

109
00:06:03,433 --> 00:06:06,200
And how long are we going
to wait?

110
00:06:06,333 --> 00:06:09,133
My daughter's mind
is going through something

111
00:06:09,300 --> 00:06:11,667
because she hasn't seen
Miguel yet.

112
00:06:12,700 --> 00:06:15,600
Chief, she feels like Miguel
is still alive.

113
00:06:19,633 --> 00:06:22,833
Chief, I'm begging you,

114
00:06:22,967 --> 00:06:25,567
show me Miguel.

115
00:06:26,767 --> 00:06:29,733
Then let's do your protocols
later on.

116
00:06:36,533 --> 00:06:37,833
Thank you.

117
00:07:04,667 --> 00:07:06,167
<i> Thank you, Chief.</i>

118
00:07:08,167 --> 00:07:10,400
I'll find a way, Clarissa.

119
00:07:10,533 --> 00:07:14,167
Your husband is a good man
and a good cop,

120
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:16,267
and he doesn't deserve this.

121
00:07:16,433 --> 00:07:19,800
That's why I'm begging you.
Just be patient.

122
00:07:23,733 --> 00:07:25,200
Okay, Chief.

123
00:07:26,733 --> 00:07:29,400
It's just really hard
because there's no closure

124
00:07:29,533 --> 00:07:30,967
to what happened to Miguel.

125
00:07:32,167 --> 00:07:33,533
Don't worry.

126
00:07:33,667 --> 00:07:36,033
I'll call you once
he's released.

127
00:07:36,167 --> 00:07:37,667
I promise...

128
00:07:37,800 --> 00:07:41,700
I'll get Miguel back to you
as soon as possible.

129
00:07:44,100 --> 00:07:45,467
Thank you.

130
00:07:45,600 --> 00:07:48,233
Cruz, please take her
to the door.

131
00:08:00,933 --> 00:08:04,100
Sir, the package has been
delivered to Delgado.

132
00:08:04,233 --> 00:08:07,433
I hope it helps
with his mission.

133
00:08:21,900 --> 00:08:23,633
<i> I wonder who owns this.</i>

134
00:08:23,767 --> 00:08:25,600
<i> Black sedan,</i>

135
00:08:25,733 --> 00:08:28,467
<i> ELS 8-0-2-5.</i>

136
00:08:47,600 --> 00:08:50,333
Peter, why did you call me?

137
00:08:52,333 --> 00:08:53,333
Here.

138
00:08:55,400 --> 00:08:56,900
I'm returning these to you.

139
00:08:58,267 --> 00:08:59,200
What?

140
00:08:59,333 --> 00:09:00,800
I gave these to you.

141
00:09:00,933 --> 00:09:02,500
I don't need it anymore.

142
00:09:05,933 --> 00:09:07,000
Why?

143
00:09:08,633 --> 00:09:10,567
I talked to Joey.

144
00:09:10,700 --> 00:09:12,800
She's with Andrew.

145
00:09:12,933 --> 00:09:14,400
I even got worried.

146
00:09:15,533 --> 00:09:17,233
They say they're following
a lead.

147
00:09:17,367 --> 00:09:18,700
What lead?

148
00:09:18,833 --> 00:09:20,633
Is this about the syndicate?

149
00:09:20,767 --> 00:09:24,133
I don't know. I didn't ask.
Joey was in a hurry.

150
00:09:24,267 --> 00:09:25,367
Are you okay?

151
00:09:26,667 --> 00:09:29,933
No matter what makeover I do,
it's useless.

152
00:09:31,133 --> 00:09:33,533
I still lose to Andrew.

153
00:09:33,667 --> 00:09:38,300
He can help Joey better
in his situation than I can.

154
00:09:38,433 --> 00:09:40,933
While here I am...

155
00:09:41,067 --> 00:09:42,567
Useless.

156
00:09:54,600 --> 00:09:56,800
Madam Delilah,
I'll take care of this!

157
00:09:56,933 --> 00:09:57,967
Okay!

158
00:09:58,100 --> 00:10:00,300
<i>There's this woman under
my radar, it's Delilah.</i>

159
00:10:00,433 --> 00:10:02,367
<i>She's the one suspected
of being in charge</i>

160
00:10:02,533 --> 00:10:04,000
<i>of drug distribution here
in Valmora.</i>

161
00:10:04,133 --> 00:10:07,200
<i>You know, if Berdugo will meet
someone here, it might be her.</i>

162
00:10:12,467 --> 00:10:13,933
Hello, good morning!

163
00:10:14,067 --> 00:10:15,300
Good morning.

164
00:10:16,933 --> 00:10:18,300
Excuse me.

165
00:10:22,667 --> 00:10:24,700
Confirmed,
Delilah is here.

166
00:10:24,833 --> 00:10:27,467
Exactly, and right next
to our villa,

167
00:10:27,600 --> 00:10:31,267
which means we can more easily
monitor her every move.

168
00:10:33,167 --> 00:10:36,400
At least, we'll know if she's
really meeting with Berdugo.

169
00:10:36,567 --> 00:10:39,733
We'll take our time
before we investigate.

170
00:10:39,867 --> 00:10:43,300
But for now, stay here
until she makes a move.

171
00:10:47,133 --> 00:10:48,467
Let's check the villa.

172
00:11:10,167 --> 00:11:13,033
We probably don't need
to pretend all the way inside,

173
00:11:13,167 --> 00:11:13,800
right?

174
00:11:13,933 --> 00:11:15,100
Of course.

175
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:18,267
Joey, don't feel awkward
with me.

176
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:21,000
That's the last thing
I want you to feel.

177
00:11:23,067 --> 00:11:25,833
- I'll just sleep on the sofa.
- No, no...

178
00:11:25,967 --> 00:11:28,267
I'll be on the sofa.

179
00:11:28,400 --> 00:11:31,433
You can have the bed.
That's great.

180
00:11:33,033 --> 00:11:35,900
And the CR, let's schedule it.

181
00:11:36,033 --> 00:11:38,700
Can I just go first
in the morning?

182
00:11:38,833 --> 00:11:40,033
In the morning?

183
00:11:40,167 --> 00:11:41,367
What about...

184
00:11:41,533 --> 00:11:43,033
What about if there's
an emergency?

185
00:11:43,167 --> 00:11:46,267
If you can't take it anymore,
your stomach hurts?

186
00:11:46,400 --> 00:11:50,267
Well, you can do it outside.
You can handle that. You're old.

187
00:11:50,400 --> 00:11:52,400
Wow. Wow, okay.

188
00:11:52,533 --> 00:11:56,567
Anyway, I'll just get our stuff
in the car.

189
00:12:00,067 --> 00:12:03,600
Joey, let's stick to the plan.

190
00:12:03,733 --> 00:12:08,000
And whatever happens to us
here while pretending,

191
00:12:08,133 --> 00:12:11,967
I want you to know
that I will protect you.

192
00:12:18,700 --> 00:12:20,033
I'll go ahead.

193
00:12:27,900 --> 00:12:29,500
Let's just follow Joey
and Andrew.

194
00:12:29,633 --> 00:12:30,767
We can help them too.

195
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:33,700
And that way, you will have
a chance with Joey.

196
00:12:33,833 --> 00:12:34,833
No need.

197
00:12:34,967 --> 00:12:37,367
I'll just look desperate
and need attention.

198
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:39,267
Instead of getting closer
to her,

199
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:42,833
I'll just keep my distance
so I can forget!

200
00:12:42,967 --> 00:12:44,700
I'll just go back
to the province.

201
00:12:44,833 --> 00:12:46,133
Are you leaving?

202
00:12:47,300 --> 00:12:48,500
Why?

203
00:12:48,667 --> 00:12:49,967
Will you miss me?

204
00:12:50,100 --> 00:12:51,033
No.

205
00:12:53,067 --> 00:12:54,933
I'll miss you.

206
00:12:55,067 --> 00:12:57,767
You're the only true friend
I've ever had here.

207
00:12:59,233 --> 00:13:00,133
Thank you.

208
00:13:03,333 --> 00:13:06,433
Thank you for all your kindness.

209
00:13:07,800 --> 00:13:10,600
Someday, I will return
the favor.

210
00:13:10,733 --> 00:13:12,867
Thank you for being
a good friend.

211
00:13:14,000 --> 00:13:16,233
I'm not because I wasn't
completely honest with you.

212
00:13:17,633 --> 00:13:19,867
You're talking to me
in Korean again.

213
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,533
What did you say?

214
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:26,033
I said I will miss the guy who
keeps calling me Oppa.

215
00:13:31,567 --> 00:13:36,867
Things will get better.
Trust me. Just be careful, okay?

216
00:13:38,033 --> 00:13:39,367
Yeah, Oppa.

217
00:13:49,467 --> 00:13:50,500
Zoey!

218
00:13:55,200 --> 00:13:56,567
Zoey, wait a minute.

219
00:14:03,433 --> 00:14:07,500
What are you doing?
Someone might see us here.

220
00:14:07,633 --> 00:14:10,433
Just relax.
I'm also a hotel guest.

221
00:14:10,567 --> 00:14:12,200
I don't think
there's something wrong

222
00:14:12,333 --> 00:14:13,867
with talking to another guest?

223
00:14:16,167 --> 00:14:17,967
What do you want?

224
00:14:18,100 --> 00:14:19,933
I want to apologize.

225
00:14:20,067 --> 00:14:21,900
For not listening to me?

226
00:14:22,033 --> 00:14:23,200
Yes,

227
00:14:24,433 --> 00:14:25,967
and if it's any help,

228
00:14:26,100 --> 00:14:28,933
we've confirmed that Delilah
is here.

229
00:14:29,100 --> 00:14:31,367
She's just in the room next
to ours.

230
00:14:31,500 --> 00:14:32,667
And?

231
00:14:34,533 --> 00:14:35,833
That's it?

232
00:14:37,733 --> 00:14:38,933
Yeah.

233
00:14:39,067 --> 00:14:43,767
I'll just give you some more
info once I get something.

234
00:14:43,900 --> 00:14:47,933
And I know you didn't like
what I did.

235
00:14:49,033 --> 00:14:53,000
And I feel like we'll get better
results if we work together,

236
00:14:53,133 --> 00:14:54,000
Zoey.

237
00:14:54,133 --> 00:14:56,733
Is it okay for your girlfriend
to share?

238
00:14:56,867 --> 00:14:58,233
We're just pretending.

239
00:14:59,700 --> 00:15:03,467
And I feel like she won't mind
if we share info.

240
00:15:16,200 --> 00:15:20,133
The guy in red,
we saw in the other room.

241
00:15:21,567 --> 00:15:24,100
He called Delilah, Boss.

242
00:15:40,033 --> 00:15:43,267
You're my ticket to getting
closer to Delilah.

243
00:15:43,400 --> 00:15:45,600
Get everything...

244
00:16:03,800 --> 00:16:05,733
Clarissa...

245
00:16:05,867 --> 00:16:07,633
what are you doing here?

246
00:16:09,867 --> 00:16:13,600
Ma'am, because I have
some work left to do.

247
00:16:13,733 --> 00:16:16,167
I thought it would be better
to finish it first.

248
00:16:17,533 --> 00:16:20,567
Clarissa, I know what happened
to your husband.

249
00:16:20,700 --> 00:16:22,600
My condolences.

250
00:16:24,767 --> 00:16:26,667
How are you doing?

251
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:30,000
It's okay, Ma'am.
I'm trying to be busy.

252
00:16:30,133 --> 00:16:32,433
You don't have to do that.

253
00:16:32,567 --> 00:16:35,667
I've assigned someone to do
your work.

254
00:16:35,800 --> 00:16:39,067
I know how hard
what you've been going through.

255
00:16:41,233 --> 00:16:43,433
Is that so, Ma'am?

256
00:16:43,600 --> 00:16:46,800
Well, sorry,
sorry for the hassle, but...

257
00:16:47,867 --> 00:16:53,467
Ma'am, it's better this way
than having to worry about

258
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:57,767
when my husband's body
will be released.

259
00:16:57,900 --> 00:17:00,033
And besides, what my daughter
said is also right.

260
00:17:00,167 --> 00:17:03,733
She said
"Life should just go on."

261
00:17:04,967 --> 00:17:07,233
I understand,

262
00:17:07,367 --> 00:17:09,533
but I got you covered here,
okay?

263
00:17:09,667 --> 00:17:13,733
I'll understand if you can't
come to the foundation for now.

264
00:17:13,867 --> 00:17:14,967
Me too,

265
00:17:15,133 --> 00:17:17,700
I might not be able to take care
of my foundation for now.

266
00:17:17,833 --> 00:17:19,433
Why, Ma'am?

267
00:17:19,567 --> 00:17:23,100
Well, Mom lost her caregiver,

268
00:17:23,233 --> 00:17:25,933
so I'll take care of her
for now.

269
00:17:26,067 --> 00:17:28,433
It's hard to find a replacement.

270
00:17:29,900 --> 00:17:32,567
Well Ma'am,
if you can't find one,

271
00:17:32,700 --> 00:17:33,867
I'm available.

272
00:17:35,067 --> 00:17:37,367
No. It's embarrassing.

273
00:17:37,500 --> 00:17:39,000
Go ahead, Ma'am.

274
00:17:39,133 --> 00:17:40,733
Please agree.

275
00:17:40,867 --> 00:17:43,133
I need this.

276
00:17:43,267 --> 00:17:46,967
It's also a way to get rid of
the sadness in my mind.

277
00:17:47,100 --> 00:17:51,200
If you agree, I'm not the only
one helping you.

278
00:17:52,533 --> 00:17:54,967
You can help me too.

279
00:18:01,400 --> 00:18:03,500
Just put it on the table.
Thank you.

280
00:18:06,400 --> 00:18:07,767
Hello there!

281
00:18:10,467 --> 00:18:12,067
Hello.

282
00:18:12,200 --> 00:18:14,733
I didn't know I had a neighbor.

283
00:18:15,800 --> 00:18:17,633
I'm Madam Delilah.

284
00:18:17,767 --> 00:18:19,033
Joey.

285
00:18:20,833 --> 00:18:23,400
Let me guess.
Room service?

286
00:18:23,567 --> 00:18:25,300
You must be alone.

287
00:18:25,433 --> 00:18:26,767
No.

288
00:18:26,900 --> 00:18:29,067
Actually, I'm with my boyfriend.

289
00:18:29,200 --> 00:18:33,967
We just got here, so I ordered
room service first.

290
00:18:34,100 --> 00:18:36,700
That's not acceptable.

291
00:18:36,833 --> 00:18:40,067
You know what,
you should enjoy this place!

292
00:18:40,200 --> 00:18:41,133
You know,

293
00:18:41,267 --> 00:18:43,800
we have camping areas here

294
00:18:43,933 --> 00:18:46,800
where you can enjoy dinner
under the stars.

295
00:18:46,933 --> 00:18:48,500
Don't worry,
I'll have that ready.

296
00:18:48,633 --> 00:18:51,400
Okay, okay. It's embarrassing.

297
00:18:51,533 --> 00:18:53,800
Besides, we don't have
any equipment because...

298
00:18:53,933 --> 00:18:55,800
No, no, no, no.
Don't think about that

299
00:18:55,967 --> 00:18:59,700
because I believe being in love
should always be celebrated

300
00:18:59,833 --> 00:19:00,967
and treasured.

301
00:19:02,300 --> 00:19:05,233
Call Francis for their camping
needs.

302
00:19:06,600 --> 00:19:09,800
You know, it's a shame.
I have an appointment later,

303
00:19:09,933 --> 00:19:12,333
but if I catch up with you
tonight,

304
00:19:12,467 --> 00:19:16,633
I hope you don't mind sharing
your story of how you met.

305
00:19:16,767 --> 00:19:19,400
Sure, okay. Thank you.

306
00:19:19,533 --> 00:19:21,533
You're welcome, my dear.

307
00:19:21,667 --> 00:19:23,267
I'll see you later, I hope.

308
00:19:23,400 --> 00:19:25,000
- See you later.
- Okay.

309
00:19:30,133 --> 00:19:31,767
So, you're Delilah.

310
00:19:54,667 --> 00:19:56,833
Why did he leave
his cell phone here?

311
00:19:56,967 --> 00:19:58,800
He's such a jerk.

312
00:20:03,400 --> 00:20:04,600
Where did you come from?

313
00:20:04,733 --> 00:20:05,700
What took you so long?

314
00:20:05,833 --> 00:20:07,600
Why would you leave
your cell phone here?

315
00:20:07,733 --> 00:20:08,633
You're too much...

316
00:20:08,767 --> 00:20:11,100
and I'm coming back.

317
00:20:11,233 --> 00:20:12,367
Exaggerated.

318
00:20:14,533 --> 00:20:16,233
Why? Is there a problem?

319
00:20:16,367 --> 00:20:18,200
Delilah left.

320
00:20:18,333 --> 00:20:19,567
She left?

321
00:20:19,700 --> 00:20:23,033
Well then, let's follow her.
Do you know where she went?

322
00:20:23,167 --> 00:20:25,000
No, I don't know.

323
00:20:25,133 --> 00:20:28,200
But I heard she'll be back
tonight.

324
00:20:28,333 --> 00:20:30,967
Then I guess there's nothing we
can do.

325
00:20:31,100 --> 00:20:32,767
There is.

326
00:20:32,900 --> 00:20:34,667
There's no one in the villa.

327
00:20:34,800 --> 00:20:37,333
We can go in,
maybe we can get a clue.

328
00:20:40,300 --> 00:20:42,133
You take care of our shipments.

329
00:20:42,267 --> 00:20:44,800
Make sure the quality
of our products.

330
00:20:44,933 --> 00:20:48,467
It's okay, Boss,
same as before.

331
00:20:48,600 --> 00:20:53,000
Tell our staff to pick me up
from home on the way to Valmora.

332
00:20:57,133 --> 00:21:00,300
Matias,
why aren't you answering?

333
00:21:00,433 --> 00:21:02,933
Boss, maybe I should just go
to Valmora?

334
00:21:03,067 --> 00:21:04,233
Why?

335
00:21:04,367 --> 00:21:07,900
<i>Castro, our contact in
the police department,</i>

336
00:21:08,033 --> 00:21:10,400
said that someone asked
about Berdugo.

337
00:21:11,467 --> 00:21:13,933
<i>Boss, maybe they're suspecting.</i>

338
00:21:14,067 --> 00:21:18,267
So there won't be any problem,
I'll meet with Delilah.

339
00:21:38,467 --> 00:21:39,700
Hurry up.

340
00:21:39,833 --> 00:21:40,800
Just wait.

341
00:21:40,933 --> 00:21:42,333
Have you eaten yet?

342
00:21:42,500 --> 00:21:44,600
Where do you want to eat first?

343
00:21:45,967 --> 00:21:48,133
- I want Japanese.
- Japanese?

344
00:21:48,267 --> 00:21:49,600
There's no Japanese here.

345
00:21:50,633 --> 00:21:54,667
- I'll have my nails done.
- That's great.

346
00:22:10,767 --> 00:22:12,333
Can you open that?

347
00:22:13,933 --> 00:22:16,667
Of course.
Watch and learn.

348
00:22:18,367 --> 00:22:21,433
I'll take care of you.

349
00:22:21,567 --> 00:22:23,533
You're all on standby here?

350
00:22:23,667 --> 00:22:26,000
I want you all to welcome
my special guest

351
00:22:26,133 --> 00:22:27,400
when he arrives.

352
00:22:30,533 --> 00:22:31,967
Yes, Madam Delilah.

353
00:22:38,933 --> 00:22:39,933
Dear...

354
00:22:40,067 --> 00:22:42,933
I knew it.
I forgot something in my safe.

355
00:22:46,767 --> 00:22:47,867
<i> Hello?</i>

356
00:22:48,000 --> 00:22:51,233
<i>- I'm done cleaning! Come on...
-</i> Come...

357
00:22:55,867 --> 00:22:57,700
What are you doing?

358
00:22:57,833 --> 00:22:59,333
Just trust me, okay?

359
00:23:14,833 --> 00:23:17,667
We should be sticking
to our characters

360
00:23:17,800 --> 00:23:19,133
so no one will catch us.

361
00:23:19,267 --> 00:23:22,033
Is the person you're talking
to trustworthy, Madam Delilah?

362
00:23:22,200 --> 00:23:24,500
When will we meet
the new supplier?

363
00:23:24,633 --> 00:23:25,733
I'll be leaving Manila soon.

364
00:23:25,867 --> 00:23:27,700
I'll be there and continue
with our plan.

365
00:23:27,833 --> 00:23:31,333
Don't worry about anything.
Nothing will go wrong here.

366
00:23:31,467 --> 00:23:33,067
- Ouch.
- Are you okay?

367
00:23:33,200 --> 00:23:34,167
No, I'm not!

368
00:23:34,300 --> 00:23:35,767
Stay here. Wait for me.

369
00:23:35,900 --> 00:23:37,133
- I'll just look for clues.
- Are you leaving me here?

370
00:23:37,267 --> 00:23:38,167
Joey, there's a safe [box] here.

371
00:23:38,300 --> 00:23:39,500
Do you know the combination
code?

372
00:23:39,633 --> 00:23:42,100
Why are you standing outside
my room?

373
00:23:42,233 --> 00:23:43,967
Check everywhere! Check inside.

374
00:23:44,100 --> 00:23:45,867
Maybe it was just the wind
earlier?

375
00:23:46,000 --> 00:23:47,533
You look scared.
